"No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, and the fundamentals point to a comfortable Republican margin of roughly fourteen points. The incumbent president is term-limited, so neither side benefits from incumbency, and no candidate-specific fundraising figures are available. No general-election polls of the state have been published, and no expert ratings exist, so the estimate rests entirely on the state's partisan lean.\n\nRecent coverage centers on the 2026 governor's race, Senate primaries, and redistricting, none of which suggests a statewide shift in presidential politics. Democratic turnout efforts in Memphis could trim the margin in a strong year, but the state's Republican advantage has been durable across cycles. On that basis, Tennessee sits in Likely Republican territory, with uncertainty wide enough to reflect the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}]}